&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenet3® is a digital knowledge management company based in Dayton, Ohio. We have deep roots in cybersecurity, system trustworthiness, and software/hardware assurance. We develop software products involving advanced machine learning and property graph representations to enhance human cognition. Tenet3 is a recognized leader in creating novel solutions for managing knowledge about complex systems. Our capabilities put data in context so that teams can generate meaningful insights. We leverage our knowledge management platform, MeTRA®, and sophisticated AI/ML tooling to rapidly build digital knowledge graphs using open data standards that make them accessible and usable across the lifecycle. Tenet3 is growing by applying our knowledge management platform to systems assurance, cybersecurity, and engineering change analyses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tenet3, our employee’s contributions are highly visible, valued, and rewarded. Be part of a team that supports both your personal and professional growth. Our team thrives in a collaborative, growth-oriented environment where we’re continuously pushing the boundaries of what’s possible. If you’re looking to work in a place that combines cutting-edge technology with a strong sense of culture and team spirit, and amazing benefits, then we are the place for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenet3 is seeking an experienced, detail-oriented Accounting Manager to lead and execute the company’s accounting and financial operations. Serving as our primary internal accounting authority, this role owns full-cycle accounting, financial reporting, government contract billing, indirect rate calculations, budgeting, forecasting, and incurred cost submissions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on individual contributor position with broad functional ownership and no initial direct reports. The ideal candidate pairs rigorous technical accounting expertise with deep federal government contracting experience. You will independently steer our accounting functions while delivering actionable, strategic financial insights directly to executive leadership to guide operational and business decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;General Accounting &amp;amp; Financial Operations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day accounting operations, including general ledger, accounts payable, accounts receivable, and payroll coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead monthly, quarterly, and year-end close processes; prepare journal entries, accruals, account reconciliations, and supporting schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce accurate financial statements compliant with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and enhance internal financial controls, accounting policies, and standard operating procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with external CPAs, auditors, and tax professionals on corporate tax planning, filings, and reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Payroll Administration and HR Coordination&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee end-to-end payroll processing to ensure accurate, timely compensation, deductions, and tax withholdings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Human Resources on onboarding, salary adjustments, benefits deductions, and DCAA-compliant timekeeping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and reconcile payroll reports, labor distribution entries, and general ledger postings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with external tax advisors and payroll vendors on quarterly/annual payroll tax filings and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Government Contract Billing &amp;amp; Administration&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, reconcile, and submit contract invoices via government platforms and commercial billing channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor contract funding thresholds, period-of-performance dates, modifications, and accounts receivable collections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with managers to verify labor allocations, direct expenses, deliverables, and contract-level profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cost Accounting, Indirect Rates &amp;amp; DCAA Compliance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, monitor, and analyze indirect cost pools and allocation bases (fringe, overhead, G&amp;amp;A) in compliance with FAR and CAS requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track direct vs. indirect cost classifications, perform rate variance analyses, and identify/segregate unallowable costs under FAR Part 31.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and update provisional billing rates; support labor rate pricing models for new contract proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support government accounting reviews, audit inquiries, and rate agreement discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;ICE Model Development &amp;amp; Incurred Cost Proposals&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently build and maintain the annual DCAA Incurred Cost Electronically (ICE) model and supporting workpapers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile indirect cost pools, allocation bases, and claimed contract costs to the general ledger and financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculate final indirect rates, document variances from provisional rates, and support DCAA incurred cost audits through final closeout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Financial Planning, Forecasting &amp;amp; Analysis&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the creation and maintenance of the annual operating budget and rolling cash-flow forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver monthly budget-to-actual variance reports, identifying financial trends, cost drivers, risks, and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dynamic financial models to assess the financial impact of business investments, staffing plans, and new contract awards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Government Contracting Accounting:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years of accounting experience, with substantial, demonstrated experience operating inside a federal government contracting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;GAAP &amp;amp; Full-Cycle Accounting:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Proven mastery of GAAP, general ledger management, month-end/year-end closes, and financial statement preparation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Payroll &amp;amp; Timekeeping Administration:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Direct experience managing or overseeing payroll processing, payroll tax compliance, and labor distribution within a DCAA-compliant timekeeping environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;DCAA Compliance &amp;amp; ICE Submission: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Direct, hands-on experience building DCAA ICE models, preparing incurred cost proposals, and supporting government audit procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Indirect Rate Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated ability to establish, calculate, and monitor indirect rate structures (fringe, overhead, G&amp;amp;A) and evaluate rate variances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Billing &amp;amp; Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/em&gt;Working knowledge of government billing systems, standard contract types (CPFF, T&amp;amp;M, FFP), and modern ERP/accounting platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Financial Modeling &amp;amp; Excel:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel (e.g., complex formulas, pivot tables, financial modeling, rate impact analysis).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;FP&amp;amp;A &amp;amp; Cash Flow Management:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Practical background in developing operating budgets, labor forecasting, and operational cash-flow projections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Autonomous Execution &amp;amp; Integrity:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently manage end-to-end accounting operations, meet critical regulatory deadlines, and handle sensitive fiscal data with total discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unanet Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/em&gt;Hands-on experience utilizing Unanet ERP for GovCon project accounting, timekeeping, billing, and indirect cost rate management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Proposal &amp;amp; Pricing Support:&lt;/em&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Experience establishing forward pricing rates, provisional billing rates, and cost volumes for federal proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-Growth/Tech Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/em&gt;Experience managing financial and accounting operations within a scaling technology, software, or defense engineering firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;FAR/CAS Mastery:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Deep familiarity with FAR Part 31 cost principles, CAS compliance, and DCAA accounting system requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field (or equivalent combination of education and directly relevant federal government contracting experience).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenet3 provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment. Equal employment opportunity applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leave of absence, compensation, and training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary for this position is based upon skill level and years of experience. Typical range is between $110,000- $130,000&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenet3® is a digital knowledge management company based in Dayton, Ohio. We have deep roots in cybersecurity, system trustworthiness, and software/hardware assurance. We develop software products involving advanced machine learning and property graph representations to enhance human cognition. Tenet3 is a recognized leader in creating novel solutions for managing knowledge about complex systems. Our capabilities put data in context so that teams can generate meaningful insights. We leverage our knowledge management platform, MeTRA®, and sophisticated AI/ML tooling to rapidly build digital knowledge graphs using open data standards that make them accessible and usable across the lifecycle. Tenet3 is growing by applying our knowledge management platform to systems assurance, cybersecurity, and engineering change analyses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tenet3, our employee’s contributions are highly visible, valued, and rewarded. Be part of a team that supports both your personal and professional growth. Our team thrives in a collaborative, growth-oriented environment where we’re continuously pushing the boundaries of what’s possible. If you’re looking to work in a place that combines cutting-edge technology with a strong sense of culture and team spirit, and amazing benefits, then we are the place for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced DevOps Engineer with a strong background in Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) and automation to serve as a technical advocate supporting our client&#39;s cloud initiatives. This role involves collaborating with development and security teams to build resilient CI/CD pipelines, optimize core cloud network topologies, and maintain proactive observability and alerting tools. You will have the opportunity to leverage your expertise in cloud orchestration, scripting, and access management, working closely with our team to deliver high-impact, secure, and repeatable cloud deployments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate would be an automation-driven systems thinker who understands that infrastructure is only as reliable as the code that provisions it. This position will bridge the gap between application development and IT operations, ensuring our client&#39;s mission-critical systems are secure, scalable, and highly available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and optimize infrastructure-as-code (IaC) for repeatable and secure cloud deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and refactor CI/CD pipelines to accelerate feature delivery, minimize risk, and reduce technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and manage observability tools, dashboards, and proactive alerting to detect and resolve issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to production issues, perform root cause analysis, and contribute to incident postmortems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with development teams to align infrastructure design with application requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document technical designs, runbooks, and standard operating procedures to ensure team alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in sprint planning and advocate for automation opportunities to improve operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize Cloud &amp;amp; DevOps Skills to:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, provision, and maintain core cloud network topologies and troubleshoot connectivity across multi-environment setups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance secrets management, access controls, and audit IAM roles/policies for least-privilege access in collaboration with security engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve visibility into cloud resource utilization and cost to support budget-aware engineering decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Technical Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of professional engineering experience in DevOps or Cloud Engineering, with a track record of identifying automation gaps, recommending IaC improvements, and troubleshooting multi-environment or hybrid setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Infrastructure &amp;amp; IaC:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in modern IaC and orchestration tools (e.g., Terraform, Kubernetes, Ansible, CloudFormation), with experience managing core cloud network topologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI/CD &amp;amp; Automation Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid experience with CI/CD systems (e.g., GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD) and strong scripting skills (e.g., Python, Bash) for automating routine tasks and reducing manual toil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability &amp;amp; Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with industry-standard observability tools (e.g., CloudWatch, Prometheus, Datadog, Grafana) to develop proactive alerts, metrics, and dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing secrets and access using tools like AWS Secrets Manager, Vault, or SSM, with a strong understanding of cloud IAM roles and least-privilege enforcement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Communication &amp;amp; Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear communication of infrastructure requirements, risks, and opportunities, with a proven ability to partner effectively with developers and IT to support secure, reliable delivery pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Education&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, information technology, systems engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tenet3, we offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support both your personal and professional well-being:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous Paid Time Off&lt;/strong&gt;: Including PTO, sick days, and floating holidays to help you recharge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health Coverage&lt;/strong&gt;: 100% paid medical, vision, and dental insurance for you and your family.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HSA Contribution: &lt;/strong&gt;Company contribution to help offset costs of the health insurance deductibles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement Plan&lt;/strong&gt;: 401(k) with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational Support&lt;/strong&gt;: Reimbursement for higher education, conferences, and self-study programs to support your continued learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disability &amp;amp; Life Insurance&lt;/strong&gt;: Short-term and long-term disability, along with life insurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Work Hours&lt;/strong&gt;: Flex time to accommodate your work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tenet3 provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment. Equal employment opportunity applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leave of absence, compensation, and training.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenet3® is a digital knowledge management company based in Dayton, Ohio. We have deep roots in cybersecurity, system trustworthiness, and software/hardware assurance. We develop software products involving advanced machine learning and property graph representations to enhance human cognition. Tenet3 is a recognized leader in creating novel solutions for managing knowledge about complex systems. Our capabilities put data in context so that teams can generate meaningful insights. We leverage our knowledge management platform, MeTRA®, and sophisticated AI/ML tooling to rapidly build digital knowledge graphs using open data standards that make them accessible and usable across the lifecycle. Tenet3 is growing by applying our knowledge management platform to systems assurance, cybersecurity, and engineering change analyses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tenet3, our employee’s contributions are highly visible, valued, and rewarded. Be part of a team that supports both your personal and professional growth. Our team thrives in a collaborative, growth-oriented environment where we’re continuously pushing the boundaries of what’s possible. If you’re looking to work in a place that combines cutting-edge technology with a strong sense of culture and team spirit, and amazing benefits, then we are the place for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an early-career Frontend Software Engineer, Front End to build reliable user-facing components using established design patterns and modern web technologies. Working under the guidance of senior engineers, this role focuses on implementing scoped product features, contributing to code quality improvements, and applying user-centered design principles. You will have the opportunity to strengthen your foundational skills in front-end development while actively participating in iterative delivery and collaborative team processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a detail-oriented developer who understands that code is only as effective as the user experience it creates. This position will bridge the gap between design systems and executable front-end components, ensuring our product features are accessible, performant, and scalable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build user-facing features using React, HTML, and CSS, following established design systems and accessibility standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the implementation and refinement of scoped tickets and user stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews by incorporating feedback and applying best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug common issues, identify performance or accessibility concerns, and raise blockers with clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend team standups, demos, and retrospectives; provide clear updates and seek feedback proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain component documentation and ensure changes are communicated clearly to teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize Modern Front-End Skills to:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement responsive, accessible UI components using React and semantic HTML/CSS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow established workflows, checklists, and coding standards in an Agile environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance overall application performance, accessibility, and UI consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Front-End &amp;amp; React Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in modern JavaScript, HTML, and CSS (including layout techniques), with direct experience building web interfaces using React and component libraries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Development Tool Familiarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Knowledge of semantic HTML, responsive design techniques, version control systems (e.g., Git/GitHub), and Agile tools (e.g., Jira, GitHub Issues).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineering Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt; 1–3 years of experience (including college internships) in frontend development, with an understanding of reusable design patterns and component architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Communication &amp;amp; Articulation:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear written and verbal communication in technical discussions, with the ability to maintain component documentation and convey technical issues clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Willingness to receive and act on feedback during code reviews, a strong desire for continuous learning, and comfort contributing in daily standups and async platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Strategic Awareness:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to debug UI issues, propose targeted solutions when blocked, and begin connecting front-end implementation choices with user needs and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Education&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, civil engineering, mathematics, physics, or a related technical field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tenet3, we offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support both your personal and professional well-being:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generous Paid Time Off&lt;/strong&gt;: Including PTO, sick days, and floating holidays to help you recharge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health Coverage&lt;/strong&gt;: 100% paid medical, vision, and dental insurance for you and your family.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HSA Contribution: &lt;/strong&gt;HSA contribution to help offset some of the deductible costs.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement Plan&lt;/strong&gt;: 401(k) with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational Support&lt;/strong&gt;: Reimbursement for higher education, conferences, and self-study programs to support your continued learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disability &amp;amp; Life Insurance&lt;/strong&gt;: Short-term and long-term disability, along with life insurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Work Hours&lt;/strong&gt;: Flex time to accommodate your work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenet3 provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment. Equal employment opportunity applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leave of absence, compensation, and training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary Range: $70,000- $80,000. Range is dependent of education, skills, and experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tenet3® is a digital knowledge management company based in Dayton, Ohio. We have deep roots in cybersecurity, system trustworthiness, and software/hardware assurance. We develop software products involving advanced machine learning and property graph representations to enhance human cognition. Tenet3 is a recognized leader in creating novel solutions for managing knowledge about complex systems. Our capabilities put data in context so that teams can generate meaningful insights. We leverage our knowledge management platform, MeTRA®, and sophisticated AI/ML tooling to rapidly build digital knowledge graphs using open data standards that make them accessible and usable across the lifecycle. Tenet3 is growing by applying our knowledge management platform to systems assurance, cybersecurity, and engineering change analyses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Work Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tenet3, our employee’s contributions are highly visible, valued, and rewarded. Be part of a team that supports both your personal and professional growth. Our team thrives in a collaborative, growth-oriented environment where we’re continuously pushing the boundaries of what’s possible. If you’re looking to work in a place that combines cutting-edge technology with a strong sense of culture and team spirit, and amazing benefits, then we are the place for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Frontend Software Engineer to drive the delivery of large, complex UI features, lead architecture and design improvements, and mentor engineers across the team. Working as a senior technical contributor, this role focuses on advancing modern front-end technologies, design systems, and user-centered engineering while contributing significantly to technical strategy. You will have the opportunity to lead major UI initiatives, promote scalable architecture and accessibility, and elevate engineering best practices across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a seasoned engineer (7+ years) who understands that front-end architecture is the bridge between technical feasibility and exceptional user experience. This position will lead complex UI initiatives, mitigate technical debt, and ensure our front-end ecosystem is performant, accessible, and built for long-term scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the implementation of large-scale frontend features with minimal oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design reusable architecture patterns and contribute to the evolution of shared tooling and design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve performance bottlenecks and accessibility issues at a systemic level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a mentor to associate and mid-level engineers, providing technical guidance, code review feedback, and pair programming support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional partners and design teams to clarify ambiguous requirements and align UI implementation with product strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence roadmap priorities through technical feasibility insights and proactive risk mitigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize Advanced Front-End Technologies to:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build interactive 2D/WebGL frontends using Pixi.js and optimize performance via Web Workers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate AI developer workflows and AI capabilities into front-end applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize applications using code splitting, lazy loading, performance profiling tools, and CI/CD testing frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
